# Godot Dialogue Manager 4 — syntax showcase
#
# In your own project the .dialogue extension sets the filetype automatically.
# This file is also used by the plugin's test suite.

## This note is exported as a translators' note (## prefix)

import "res://levels/town/snippets.dialogue" as snippets

using GameState

~ start

Nathan: Hey, welcome to the Dialogue Manager! [ID:WELCOME]
Nathan: I can speak in [b]bold[/b], [i]italics[/i], or [color=red]colour[/color].
Nathan: I can pick [[this|or this|or even this]] at random.
Nathan: You have {{GameState.apple_count}} [if GameState.apple_count == 1]apple[else]apples[/if]!
Nathan: Pauses are easy: [wait=1]...[speed=3]and now I'm talking faster![speed=1]
Nathan: Things can happen [$> emote("wave")]right in the middle of a line.
Coco: Meow.

# Simultaneous dialogue
Nathan: This is a regular line of dialogue.
| Coco: And I'll say this line at the same time!
| {{GameState.other_speaker}}: Even my name can come from a variable.

# Weighted random lines
Nathan: I will always say this.
% Nathan: And then I might say this
%3 Nathan: This one is three times as likely as the line above
% Nathan: Or maybe this

# Random blocks
%
	Nathan: This is the first random block.
	Nathan: Still the first block.
% Nathan: This is the other possible outcome.

if GameState.has_met_nathan == false
	$> GameState.animate("Nathan", "Wave")
	Nathan: Hi, I'm Nathan.
	$> GameState.has_met_nathan = true

Nathan: What would you like to know?

- Tell me more about this dialogue editor [if not GameState.asked_editor /]
	$> GameState.asked_editor = true
	Nathan: Well, you write dialogue like a script...
	=>< snippets/banter
	Nathan: ...and that was some imported banter!
- What's your favourite colour?
	if GameState.favourite_colour == null
		Nathan: I'd say blue. It's calming.
	else
		Nathan: I already told you — it's blue!
	- Blue [if GameState.favourite_colour == "blue" /]
		Nathan: Great minds think alike!
	- Something else => start
- Nothing, thanks => END

match GameState.question_count
	when 0
		Nathan: You haven't asked anything yet!
	when > 5
		Nathan: Wow, you're full of questions.
	else
		Nathan: Keep them coming.

while GameState.question_count < 3
	Nathan: The count is {{GameState.question_count}}.
	$> GameState.question_count += 1

# v3-style lines still work (set/do are deprecated in favour of $>)
set GameState.counter = GameState.counter + 1
do something_here()

Nathan: That's everything! [next=auto]
=> END

~ second_cue
Nathan: You can jump straight to a cue, too.
=> END!
